From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:50:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_ppe: bind flows from their first packets

The PPE reports an unbound flow to the CPU for binding once it has seen
30 packets of it within a second.  A new TCP connection reaches that
rate in its first round trips of slow start, while it sends its packets
in bursts at line rate, so the bind usually takes effect in the middle
of a burst.  The PPE then forwards the rest of the burst ahead of the
packets it had already passed to the CPU.  Towards a WED device the CPU
path goes through mac80211 and the driver's TX queues, and those packets
reach the station after later ones: the sender takes them as lost and
cuts its congestion window while it is still small.

Report flows for binding from their first packets, so that they move to
the PPE before their bursts grow.  The threshold only decides when a
flow of the flow table moves to the PPE, not which flows are offloaded;
flows below 30 packets per second are now bound as well.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
@@ -1092,7 +1092,11 @@ void mtk_ppe_start(struct mtk_ppe *ppe)
 	      FIELD_PREP(MTK_PPE_BIND_LIMIT1_NON_L4, 1);
 	ppe_w32(ppe, MTK_PPE_BIND_LIMIT1, val);
 
-	val = FIELD_PREP(MTK_PPE_BIND_RATE_BIND, 30) |
+	/* Report flows for binding from their first packets: a later bind
+	 * lands in a burst, and the PPE forwards the rest of it ahead of the
+	 * packets still on the CPU path.
+	 */
+	val = FIELD_PREP(MTK_PPE_BIND_RATE_BIND, 1) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(MTK_PPE_BIND_RATE_PREBIND, 1);
 	ppe_w32(ppe, MTK_PPE_BIND_RATE, val);
 
